fix GC: record young-source edges in the remembered set too (#34 missed-edge).

fix's generational minor GC has an unsound write-barrier fast-path in gcRecordEdge:
it bails when the edge SOURCE is currently young ("source young -> not old->young").
But a young source can be PROMOTED to old in the SAME minor cycle while its young
referent is not, after which that old->young edge has no remembered-set entry -> the
minor mark (which stops at old objects and relies wholly on the remset for old->young
reachability) misses the live young child -> it is swept. Detector build: the
"minor mark not closed -- missed edge" panic. Release build: a live object is freed,
the token-keyed thunk-memo/attr caches are invalidated every collect, and the whole
draw-heavy screen graph re-forces from scratch -> a per-frame eval death-spiral
(40ms -> tens of seconds). Draw-heavy per-frame young allocation (Bad Apple's HUD, the
Gallant/Spleen info screens' pixel-surface `//` merges) triggers it.

Removing the young-source early-out records young sources in the remset too. This is
STRICTLY CONSERVATIVE -- the remset becomes a superset, so the minor mark can only be
MORE complete, never less; a young source that never tenures is harmless (the minor
already visits marked young objects, and markRemsetSource is idempotent). The remset is
cleared each minor, so the only cost is a larger remset on draw-heavy frames. This lets
the badge use the fast MINOR collect (Engine.collectNow) instead of a full major every
frame-batch, so there are no periodic ~48ms GC pauses. See the badge memo
fix-gc-missed-edge-rootcause and pkgs/badge/nix-badge/fixeval.zig.

--- a/src/runtime/heap.zig
+++ b/src/runtime/heap.zig
@@ -2038,7 +2038,6 @@
     pub inline fn gcRecordEdge(self: *ObjectHeap, source: ObjectId, referent: Value) void {
         if (!self.collection.collect_enabled) return;
         const ref_id = gcHeapId(referent) orelse return;
         if (!self.gcIsYoung(ref_id)) return; // referent already old
-        if (self.gcIsYoung(source)) return; // source young → not old→young
         // Dropping an old→young edge permits a live young object to be swept
         // during the next minor collection. The remembered set is therefore
         // correctness metadata, not an optional optimization.
